        "id": 61711,
        "name": "Ronway",
        "username": "Ronway",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ronway/{size}/1856_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-04-25T13:36:13.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Heroes&nbsp;cannot use the same power two times in a single turn even if&nbsp;they are able to use multiple powers. Now if there&nbsp;two copies of the same card out, such as Tempest with two Cleansing Downpours, then he could use both of them if he has a way of activating a second power such as Embolden from Fanatic.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>a. All Living Rockslides would act, so each would deal H-2 damage to all non-villain targets. So if two Living Rockslides were in play than the heroes would be dealt damage twice, once by each of them.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>b) Her limbs are not considered part of her. And yes if you have&nbsp;multiple Mountainous Carapace's reduction do stack with Akash'Bhuta, so she would have a minus two damage dealt to her if there are two Carapace's&nbsp;in play.</p>",
        "post_number": 2,
        "post_type": 1,
